{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20","id":1457097,"title":"Are there traces of the so-called \"Second Inquisition\" in V20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-18T05:47:11-07:00","id":1457097,"title":"Are there traces of the so-called \"Second Inquisition\" in V20?","content":"Maybe this will get covered in the Second Inquisiton book or has been mentioned and I didn\u2019t notice, but I was flicking through V20 a while back and looking through the witch-hunter section. The Arcanum and the Society of Leopold are regular hunters, but the others stood out to me and I just realised why.<br /> <br /> Because the NSA and organised crime syndicates were being manipulated behind the scenes. A handful of agency high ups were shown behind the shroud, thinking they were seeing an alternate dimension full of &quot;negative bodies&quot; (clearly where &quot;blank bodies&quot; came from). Then they get supplied with a scanner in which vampires appear exactly like wraiths (which is very interesting, but another topic). Now they think they're fighting against an invasion of body snatching extradimensional beings.<br /> Meanwhile groups like the mafia were approached by \u201cangels\u201d who turned them against their vampire leaders. These angels seem remarkably like they may be an organised group of Caitiff.<br /> I haven\u2019t had the chance to read Hunters Hunted I or II, so there could be more hunter groups like this<br /> <br /> It seems in recent history there was a supernatural force collecting pawns and nudging them into place. Or maybe multiple forces, perhaps working together or maybe their unrelated plans just got away from them when they collided and the hunter groups noticed each other.<br /> <br /> Could be Hunter: the Reckoning. Could be antediluvians. Could be a regular bunch of vampires whose schemes got out of control. Sect wars gone wrong, perhaps. Could be members of a faction within a certain global conspiracy who could get access to totally-not-magical hypertech that wants all vampires dead, like, yesterday. (I mean it probably shouldn\u2019t be the actions of another splat, but I seem to recall that the aim is a cohesive world of darkness, so)<br /> Could be all of them and more. It\u2019s Masquerade, the conspiracies have conspiracies have conspiracies, after all.<br /> <br /> Either way, by the present day it seems these groups have started to notice each other and exchange information (although without a doubt they lie, disregard given information as nonsense, hide stuff and stab each other in the back as much as their targets).<br /> And so the vampires dub this \u201ccooperation\u201d the Second Inquisition, and like the first one it\u2019s a totally manageable situation except for the fact that your fellow kindred are happy to point them in your direction if it benefits them.<br /> <br /> I suppose powerful supernatural influence would also explain the efficiency of such a patchwork \u201corganisation\u201d and a SchreckNet breach, though I don\u2019t think the latter is necessary. I'm not sure the first one is necessary either, vampires have plenty of idiots who are greatly talented when it comes to screwing their whole species over by being selfish bastards who overestimate themselves and refuse to learn.<br /> <br /> Do you think this will come up, or am I seeing things? Because there\u2019s some mysteries here and I haven't seen the answers to them (and honestly, maybe they should be left mysteries to play with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":".  typos and autocorrect 08-18-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T06:39:11-07:00","id":1457099,"title":"","content":"This sounds like a great idea for a campaign with hunters as the main antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T07:24:21-07:00","id":1457100,"title":"","content":"Have you read Hunters Hunted II? It's a solid book with plenty of ideas.<br /> <br /> as for the SI<br /> It can't be overstated how much of a political and logistical issue it would be for the various hunter factions to unite to the extent that the SI implies, without even getting into the barriers that V5 removed (The Vampires simply had better tools for dealing with organized hunters before V5; Obfuscate, Auspex and Dominate were all much, much stronger)<br /> <br /> 1- You can't have the entirity of an Agency like the CIA or FBI go after vampires, because these organizations have information available to the public; Not only would the heads of these organizations fear reprisals from vampires, but they very much benefit from the corruption that vampires bring about. The United States can't even get good public transportation because of the Car lobby, now imagine US officials endorsing the hunts of people who got them their jobs, bought their homes and whom spend millions on them per anum. And they're not even getting good publicity for it. It's not happening.<br /> 2- Yes, Rogue members of these big organizations can branch off and do work in secret, but this severely limits funding and how big they can get. They're also not going to have much of a sense of trust, so they're not likely to get in touch with rogue cells from other big groups, especially those outside their home nation. In the real world, military and intelligence alliances do not work well out of a reluctance to share information, just imagine how that'd work out with rogue fragments of big organizations.<br /> 3- The SoL, the premier hunters, would be considered a terrorist organization, so they wouldn't have great relations with Big-Gov types. They're also religious quacks, so no dealing with the Arcanum.<br /> 4- Technocrats and lupines can win battles against vampires, but they're doomed to lose wars and they know it.<br /> <br /> Thematically. Hunters have always been underdogs. It gets weird when suddenly the hunters are big government and they know what they're doing and they're outfitted with weapons from Blade. Which is a shame because V20 did great in adding diversity to hunters, and now they're a nebulous blob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-18-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T08:25:27-07:00","id":1457102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457099#post1457099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a great idea for a campaign with hunters as the main antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m kind of in love with the idea of an espionage campaign. Either hunter faction vs hunter faction or vampire vs hunter from either angle.<br /> Infiltrating, finding all the links in this patchwork mess of alliances and factions, identifying the weak ones and turning the enemy against each other. The humans struggle not to get caught by a bunch of predators with mind reading and brainwashing powers. The vampires have to find strategies to position and track their mortal pawns or fall back on blood magic and the blush of life to pass for human and do it themselves. Possession and Astral Projection are useful here, actually. Accidentally making emotional connections with the enemy and the whole bloody mess that follows... (How many members of these organisations would sell their fellows out for immortality and superpowers, I wonder?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457100#post1457100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read Hunters Hunted II? It's a solid book with plenty of ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven\u2019t had time to read it yet.<br /> <br /> The SI is absolutely too organised and bland. Ether &quot;the Second Inquisition&quot; should be the name for a time period between V20 and V5 that saw a hike in unusually devestating hunter attacks that shifted kindred society around a bit, or a blanket name for all the active hunter factions (who should all have different methods and motivations).<br /> I love Hunter: the Vigil from over in Chronicles, so having more hunters to play with is fun and I\u2019m not be sorry to see them get a bit more attention, even if I disagree with the execution and need to do heavy editing.<br /> <br /> 1- True, which adds some interesting layers to the hunter side of things because at some point you\u2019ll learn your bosses are absolutely compromised and you\u2019re surrounded by the enemy. Also gives incentive to sell out to the undead yourself. And if you don\u2019t, your friends will.<br /> <br /> There was a reason why V20 kept the government hunters as a small faction of the NSA who didn\u2019t reach out to the other agencies. I suppose the SchreckNet breach was meant to give a reason for them to reach out, but honestly that seems like it would lead to a lot of mysterious job vacancies and assassinations for any hunters involved.<br /> If there\u2019s a genuine Second Inquisiton, vampire fingerprints should be all over the place (plus some more the fucked up stuff that\u2019s 100% mortal human)<br /> <br /> 2- Also true, which is where fun can be had on the vampire side of the equation. Or in playing one of two factions within the \u201ccoalition\u201d sabotaging or spying on each other.<br /> If such cooperation is succeeding, that success indicates a puppetmaster behind the curtain and it's heavily implied many hunter groups began because of such itnterference. That itself might be a hydra situation. You take down one methuselah that was manipulating a hunter cell, and it turns out that that did nothing because the other cells are all being controlled by other things.<br /> <br /> 3- I think the SoL are probably the most volatile part of any coalition of hunters. If one accepts the SI as an actual organisation, these guys are going to be the ones who make it fall apart.<br /> <br /> 4- I doubt the Technocracy is going to make any big moves against the vampires, they\u2019ve got better things to do. Reading about the NSA just made me think of the Progenitors. I suspect it'd have to be a rogue agent or two getting impatient wanting a vampire pogrom, and I haven't gotten far enough into Mage to judge accurately, but I don't think the Technocracy would approve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thematically. Hunters have always been underdogs. It gets weird when suddenly the hunters are big government and they know what they're doing and they're outfitted with weapons from Blade. Which is a shame because V20 did great in adding diversity to hunters, and now they're a nebulous blob. </div> </div> </div>I like both. Plus you can be the underdog from within a large corrupt organisation. The SI as a kindred death machine superpower is dull, but a fragile cooalition of underdogs in a very dangerous, corrupt world who may - in trying to fight back - be pawns of something <i>worse</i>... that appeals to me greatly. But yeah, at the moment it's a nebulous blob which is absolutely a downturn in quality and a loss of interesting plot ideas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T09:53:38-07:00","id":1457107,"title":"","content":"The groundwork for the SI was laid as far back as 2e, as many of the organizations involved in it started there, such as the SAD.<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457102#post1457102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI is absolutely too organised and bland. Ether &quot;the Second Inquisition&quot; should be the name for a time period between V20 and V5 that saw a hike in unusually devestating hunter attacks that shifted kindred society around a bit, or a blanket name for all the active hunter factions (who should all have different methods and motivations).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the second option. It explains this in the books.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition isn't a huge monolithic organization, and hell, it's not even a term they call themselves. It's a term the Kindred use, coined by a Toreador neonate, about the movement of Hunters going on in the world in modern times. Otherwise, they are all kinds of different organizations, some working together and some not, doing their things and having their own goals and such. There is definitely some interconnected work going on in places, but there's also Scully and Mulder looking into stuff as much as there is a General Eiling plotting to off Superman in there doing their own things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T12:01:03-07:00","id":1457119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457107#post1457107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The groundwork for the SI was laid as far back as 2e, as many of the organizations involved in it started there, such as the SAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I think SAD lays the groundwork of why there shouldn't be an SI. SAD are small-scale and eventually get the plug pulled on them, forcing them to do things in secret. Even though they're techincally the man, they're still very much underdogs who're going crazy with what they're up against. SAD are cool and they fit in with the other hunter groups (thematically, I'm not saying they're having tea parties, that'd be insanely stupid) <br /> The SI on the otherhand are big and faceless and aren't burdened by hassles like logistics, logic, reason, good storytelling, or even a compelling vampire conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T23:56:45-07:00","id":1457186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457119#post1457119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI on the otherhand are big and faceless and aren't burdened by hassles like logistics, logic, reason, good storytelling, or even a compelling vampire conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right about this. I feel that any hypothetical Second Inquisition would be most burdened by one of Vampires' greatest achievements - the Masquerade. Exactly how is the initiation into the SI supposed to work? The mortals in the Modern Nights are wholly under the stranglehold of not believing in the supernatural <i>at all</i> (especially if the Technocracy's influence is considered as applying), much less a Vampire society like the Camarilla. Be it members of strike teams, investigators, directors, or communication specialists...all of these mortals are initially predisposed to disbelieve, doubt, and ridicule the idea of Vampires existing.<br /> <br /> The only possibility that comes to my mind is capturing Vampires and showing them to potential SI members. But this idea is kind of ridiculous - being shown one Vampire does not really convince a person that there is an entire society of them that can and should be fought. Also - the logistics of such an initiation would be limited; only so many mortals could become involved.<br /> And such an undertaking would give the Camarilla Vampires clear trails to follow and targets to strike at, as it is a clear, immediate, and distinct danger to the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457102#post1457102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4- I doubt the Technocracy is going to make any big moves against the vampires, they\u2019ve got better things to do. Reading about the NSA just made me think of the Progenitors. I suspect it'd have to be a rogue agent or two getting impatient wanting a vampire pogrom, and I haven't gotten far enough into Mage to judge accurately, but I don't think the Technocracy would approve.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a paragraph in the Revised New World Order Convention Book when it is discussed that Tremere Vampires are considered by the NWO to be stable in their approach to magic, and they are deemed as not worth the effort and resources it would take to oppose them. Which I guess could be the NWO's way of saying that they could work together or tolerate each other, at least. The NWO might just be shy like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-19-2021, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T02:50:20-07:00","id":1457195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457100#post1457100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- The SoL, the premier hunters, would be considered a terrorist organization, so they wouldn't have great relations with Big-Gov types. They're also religious quacks, so no dealing with the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checking - as from memory didn't the SoL get re-recognised by the Catholic Church structures. If this memory is correct, then they would also be part of the Big-Gov types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T04:14:00-07:00","id":1457198,"title":"","content":"In which edition? <br /> As much as the pope exists as a political entity, the modern catholic church doesn't have that much sway, at least in comparison to a government working in it's own territory. The church is more &quot;An influentual billionaire&quot; in terms of power. In terms of influence, a lot of Catholics ignore the Pope (Christians in general ignore a lot of Jesus. Turn the other cheek) <br /> <br /> Now, yeah, the church can give the SoL a few billions of funding. But they're really limited in what else they can do. Give out some Vatican passports? No that's a diplomatic incident waiting to happen. Get more recruits? Eh... the more people involved, the messier things get and the easier time vampires will have connecting the dots. It wouldn't be too hard for Vampires to intercede in Vatican politics if the CC ever threw a lot of weight behind the vampire hunt. Vampires would have more trouble if Elon Musk started going after them (and he wouldn't since, y'know, he's obviously on the side of vampires)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T04:29:35-07:00","id":1457200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457186#post1457186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a paragraph in the Revised New World Order Convention Book when it is discussed that Tremere Vampires are considered by the NWO to be stable in their approach to magic, and they are deemed as not worth the effort and resources it would take to oppose them. Which I guess could be the NWO's way of saying that they could work together or tolerate each other, at least. The NWO might just be shy like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been the general Technocracy stance on vampires since pretty much the start of Mage 2e. They see that most vampires live in a structured society that's extremely dedicated towards keeping existence of their kind secret (even if the vast majority of the Union couldn't tell you anything about the Camarilla, [older] Anarchs, and other smaller Sects or even independent Princes that put a lot of stock in the Masquerade). Even if in the long run the Technocrats want to wipe out the vampires, they have no reason to bother until much bigger threats are dealt with.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons it's going to be hard to link the Union to the Second Inquisition, is that the Technocracy's whole approach was to avoid what happened with Firstlight: disrupting vampire society such that the central authorities no longer have the power to contain the more troublesome members. The Camarilla pulling back, the Anarchs growing in number resulting in lots of small breaches due to their laxer rules enforcement, the splintering of the Tremere.... it's all stuff the Technocrats don't want to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T05:23:34-07:00","id":1457205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457200#post1457200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been the general Technocracy stance on vampires since pretty much the start of Mage 2e. They see that most vampires live in a structured society that's extremely dedicated towards keeping existence of their kind secret (even if the vast majority of the Union couldn't tell you anything about the Camarilla, [older] Anarchs, and other smaller Sects or even independent Princes that put a lot of stock in the Masquerade). Even if in the long run the Technocrats want to wipe out the vampires, they have no reason to bother until much bigger threats are dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately I see no reasons really why the Technocracy would want to wipe out Vampires overall. Yes, there is the fact that Vampires drink blood\u2026but then there are Technocrats (the Syndicate especially) who are involved in the criminal underworld directly, for example. Or there probably have been Technocrats who contributed to wars and hostilities between countries, or did not do enough (if anything) to stop them. I see these two activities as much worse than the need to drink blood. And it has to be noted that Vampires do not have to kill to drink blood - in fact, many (if not most) Vampires establish Herds.<br /> <br /> Then there is the whole \u2018Reality Deviant\u2019 issue, but I see this more as a working term that is applied to particularly troublesome or stupid Tradition or Nephandi Mages. Consider that they might be using the term for example to strengthen their Mind Effects against Mystic Mages they deemed to be antagonists. Or they might galvanize their Extraordinary through the use of such a category. I do not really see how it could be applied to Vampires - a person cannot be simply considered a Reality Deviant because they have supernatural powers. This would be going too far and at most very young or inexperienced Technocrats would hold on to such an outlook.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Vampires have great influence and control over the societies and institutions of mundane humans. Also, the insights and wisdom of Vampires (especially the older and the ancient ones) cannot simply be disregarded, and much can be learned from Vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457200#post1457200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons it's going to be hard to link the Union to the Second Inquisition, is that the Technocracy's whole approach was to avoid what happened with Firstlight: disrupting vampire society such that the central authorities no longer have the power to contain the more troublesome members. The Camarilla pulling back, the Anarchs growing in number resulting in lots of small breaches due to their laxer rules enforcement, the splintering of the Tremere.... it's all stuff the Technocrats don't want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the primary reasons why I think Technocracy would never support the SI is that they are mundane humans with limited knowledge of the supernatural who are not in any of the main Nightfolk factions (Traditions, Technocracy etc.) Even the simplest Tradition Acolyte probably knows that they are not to speak about the supernatural openly; and the more they come to know, the more they are informed about the importance of secrecy and the consequences of not abiding by it.<br /> <br /> Any SI member, on the other hand, follows no guidelines (other than maybe a very thin &quot;the higher-ups don't want it&quot;) and has no attitude in regard to the gravity of keeping supernatural matters away from the public. This is especially important for the Technocracy, as much of their influence, power, plans, and capabilities come directly from the scientific and skeptical (towards mysticism and the supernatural) outlook that they have largely enforced on the societies and cultures of mundane humans. A hypothetical scenario of the Masquerade shattering would be a huge setback and defeat for the Technocracy, as it would galvanize the mundane humans with an overall belief in the supernatural, religion, and mysticism. Not to mention the destabilization of existing societies, outlooks, beliefs, and institutions of mundane humans.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs the SI by default contributes towards such a scenario, I think the Technocracy would be hostile towards the SI. I guess they could recruit some of them as Sympathizers, but this consideration is quite superfluous \u2013 nothing really makes SI members more worthy or capable as Sympathizers, compared to other mundane humans of similar skills and aptitudes. I guess some Technocrats could take pity on them (after all, they are in over their heads for being involved in an anti-Vampire conspiracy) and try to save some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-19-2021, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T05:44:17-07:00","id":1457206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457200#post1457200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been the general Technocracy stance on vampires since pretty much the start of Mage 2e. They see that most vampires live in a structured society that's extremely dedicated towards keeping existence of their kind secret (even if the vast majority of the Union couldn't tell you anything about the Camarilla, [older] Anarchs, and other smaller Sects or even independent Princes that put a lot of stock in the Masquerade). Even if in the long run the Technocrats want to wipe out the vampires, they have no reason to bother until much bigger threats are dealt with.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons it's going to be hard to link the Union to the Second Inquisition, is that the Technocracy's whole approach was to avoid what happened with Firstlight: disrupting vampire society such that the central authorities no longer have the power to contain the more troublesome members. The Camarilla pulling back, the Anarchs growing in number resulting in lots of small breaches due to their laxer rules enforcement, the splintering of the Tremere.... it's all stuff the Technocrats don't want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was some material in Revised however that after the whole Ravnos/Bangladesh fiasco the Technocracy was starting to take the threat of vampires more seriously. The thing survived nukes being dropped on it and was only finally dropped by a quadruple orbital solar reflector and they wanted to be sure nothing like that would ever happen again.<br /> <br /> Ironically though, if you take the aftertext of the Week of Nightmares as canon, mass slaughter of an Antediluvian\u2019s line is actually what wakes them up; so a full fledged pogram against vampires would ironically hasten the coming of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> I know that\u2019s been somewhat retconned with the latest \u201ccyclical Gehenna\u201d deal vs. the previous singular end times event, but it\u2019s still something to consider in terms of SI type fallout.<br /> <br /> For the record, I use the SI more as a \u201ctime period\u201d rather than an organization. Hunter activity is on the rise because modern technology and the surveillance state is making vampires easier to identify; but it\u2019s not coordinated, just facilitated.<br /> <br /> Humans are, by nature, conspiracy theorists; are brains are built for pattern recognition and will build patterns even where none exist.<br /> <br /> Vampires are PARANOID conspiracy theorists, so when hunter attacks are on the rise because technology is making their job easier... some of them are going to reach the conclusion that it\u2019s an organized effort; a massive secret organization out to get them... an Inquisition 2.0 (and yes, I am almost positive whatever fledging or neonate first came up with it definitely used \u201ctwo point oh\u201d and it was only when an elder finally had to deign talk about it that it got called the Second Inquisition).<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s mostly what it is... a few big strikes by larger groups (often with Kindred help; ex. Vienna) that aren\u2019t actually coordinating with each other (Vienna, London and the one in Germany? where the prince was burned in the street occurred years apart in different countries... a few years is an eyeblink to immortals but six months is alifetime in mortal politics) coupled with a general rise in independent hunters (say 3 serious hunters hit a city in a decade instead of 2) and the vampires are jumping at the shadows claiming its The Second Inquisition out to get them... Panic everybody, surrender your rights to the elites who will guide us through this time of crisis and surely have your best interests at heart and aren\u2019t just exploiting events for their own benefit.<br /> <br /> Vampires are often depressingly human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T07:04:35-07:00","id":1457209,"title":"","content":"<br /> Top down justice does not and cannot exist. The concept is utterly inimical to the idea of Vampire:The Masquerade. Vampires are not a wrongly persecuted minority. They're The Man. Even the most petty and disadvantaged vampire is a boss among men. Two of the most basic innate abilities of a vampire are to steal the life-resource of people and then to redistribute these resources to create a few loyal slaves.<br /> <br /> It can't be understated how little incentive most people have, especially concering those in power, to actively go after vampires. We sadly don't live in a world where politicians prioritize doing the right things. The ones who do aren't successful and are lambasted by the media to keep them out of office. Scientists have been discussing the effects of climate change for 50 years on a factual basis, yet our response has been hilariously inadequate. Why? Well there's that sweet-sweet oil/coal money! And that's just the biggest offender. There's the drug companies, the tech companies, the food companies, the people who build cars, anyone related to finance... even if you aren't living in some chucklefuck country where bribes are legal, there are still legal avenues for politicians to get into bed with the money. How many politicians end up with high end jobs after they cease their governmental position? Then there's the politicians that came from X industry and serve mostly to deregulate X industry....<br /> <br /> If you're in power, the vampires are on your side. If you're not bothered by the oil money, the bomb money, the opiate money, or the sugar money, why would you be bothered by Vampire money? And it's not like you can take one group down in isolation. Attack Oil and the Oil companies, the Car companies who rely on them, the plastic companies, and the coal companies that see oil as a brother will screw you. Vampires are even messier because they're involved in everything. The elite have a class consience, and they'll never go against vampires because of it. Conversely, vampires will avoid targeting the elite. <br /> <br /> This is why Hunters have always been underdogs. They're people who have lost, have nothing to lose, are fringe extremists or are otherwise crazy. Every single group prior to V5 fit that bill, other than some of the earliest SAD stuff (which, y'know, evolved appropriately)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-19-2021, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T15:45:25-07:00","id":1457233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457209#post1457209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're in power, the vampires are on your side. If you're not bothered by the oil money, the bomb money, the opiate money, or the sugar money, why would you be bothered by Vampire money? And it's not like you can take one group down in isolation. Attack Oil and the Oil companies, the Car companies who rely on them, the plastic companies, and the coal companies that see oil as a brother will screw you. Vampires are even messier because they're involved in everything. The elite have a class consience, and they'll never go against vampires because of it. Conversely, vampires will avoid targeting the elite.<br /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of mine suggested the biggest bribe the Carmarilla and the Sabbat can put on the table means that it would be remarkably easy to subvert kine goverments.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you stop hunting us I will make you immortal. You will never die.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Top that enron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T00:39:07-07:00","id":1457253,"title":"","content":"They don't even need to do that.<br /> A lot of vampires have more money than they know what to do with. You support the vampire? Money goes to you. You don't support the Vampire? Money goes to your opponents, any media willing to be critical of you, any lawsuits filed against you, and your dirty secrets are up in the air.<br /> One very good advantage Vampires have over normal rich folk is Ghouls. Now, Offering your supporters immortality is, for the most part, a bad idea. You never need to reveal you're a vampire, and Ghouls are a masquerade Liability, especially when it comes to high profile figures. The real wonder of Ghouls is their absolute willingness to do anything to please their master. Vampires can find ghouls that can cater to any desire, no matter how sick and twisted. Enough blood addiction and anyone with low willpower will happily allow themselves to be abused for the master.<br /> <br /> Specialists like<b> Tzmisce</b> and <b>Malkavians</b> really excel. Not only can Tzmisce provide custom products, they can also deform people and then hold their treatment hostage. The Malkavians can really just drive people insane. Death is less worrisome than losing one's faculties. Strategic use of <i>Passion</i> can ruin careers and families, and <i>Haunting</i> is ample warning that one needs to do as they're told. Dementation easily discredits any victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T02:51:34-07:00","id":1457254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary;n1457253<br /> Specialists like [B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzmisce[/B] and <b>Malkavians</b> really excel. Not only can Tzmisce provide custom products, they can also deform people and then hold their treatment hostage. The Malkavians can really just drive people insane. Death is less worrisome than losing one's faculties. Strategic use of <i>Passion</i> can ruin careers and families, and <i>Haunting</i> is ample warning that one needs to do as they're told. Dementation easily discredits any victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, you don't need dementation to ruin a target's sanity (or make it seem so.) Creative uses of dominate to fuck with memories and leave odd subliminal messages. Auspex to put voices in their head. Obfuscate leads to &quot;hauntings&quot;, &quot;hearing voices&quot;, messages appearing from nowhere and the furniture mysteriously moving around when your back is turned. Obtenebration, 'cause shadows do not move on their own (many people are terrified of the dark).<br /> Protean and animalism: are animals <i>supposed</i> to act like that? Why do they only act odd in front of you??<br /> <br /> Presence and a special interest means the Brujah and Toreador are specialists in whipping up support you... Or taking it away.<br /> <br /> And then there's the fact that the average mortal defaults to low willpower, because the world is awful. If the blood sucking parasites with the fair advantage controlling your society and exploiting you are undead or mortal, that won't change much. You won't like it, sometimes there will be uprisings that replace the tyrant with a new tyrant, but mostly it's meh. Part of the secret behind the Cam's success as a sect, it's the one to which new vampires adjust most easily from human life: in the with the new boss, same as the old boss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-20-2021, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T03:19:04-07:00","id":1457256,"title":"","content":"Also, most people don't want power over others, they want enough power to secure comfort and safety and positive emotions and whatever.<br /> Those who seek excess power (and keep it) are typically personalities far more inclined to corruption and are more comfortable screwing people over for their own gain. You get well intentioned people who seek power to counter that, but the in-crowd is already a coalition of the 1% and their lackeys. Getting anti-vampire measures implemented gets more resistance the higher in the human hierarchy you go, and the superpowered immortals have more to offer to the selfish than you.<br /> <br /> If the 1% turn against the hand that feeds them then that's worrying, because that means something is offering a better deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-20-2021, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T07:39:33-07:00","id":1457266,"title":"","content":"I felt Hunters Hunted II kind of crapped on the NSA and SAD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T09:10:33-07:00","id":1457273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457266#post1457266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt Hunters Hunted II kind of crapped on the NSA and SAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was entirely fair. Probably not harsh enough. <br /> Suggesting the NSA is effective is very bold, nevermind their capability to locate a paranoid race of beings that are supposedly masters of deception... because they're obviously talking about vampire stuff on the phone right? surely not LARPERS or people really into RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T06:36:26-07:00","id":1457330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457266#post1457266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt Hunters Hunted II kind of crapped on the NSA and SAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, can you remind us of how SAD/NSA faired over each edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T15:31:42-07:00","id":1457353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457330#post1457330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, can you remind us of how SAD/NSA faired over each edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The NSA used to have a big idea of how vampires worked and existed due to one of its Generals organizing a bunch of vampire hunting information and starting a genuine cleaning up. Then he died of natural casues,; they found his notes, and then they all hid them because they were the work of a madman. So the NSA is back to ground zero in terms of knowing anything about vampires.<br /> <br /> 2. The SAD has been incorporated into the mainstream FBI and put on hunting serial killers rather than the supernatural. It also had all of its leadership fired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T03:21:10-07:00","id":1457378,"title":"","content":"2- That sounds... completely reasonable. Just imagine it.<br /> &quot;Hey Frank, you're using millions of taxpayer dollary-doos for what?&quot; <br /> &quot;Well we're.... Hunting Vampires&quot; <br /> &quot;....&quot;<br /> &quot;They avoid tax&quot;<br /> &quot;....&quot;<br /> &quot;They have mind control powers&quot;<br /> &quot;....&quot;<br /> &quot;look, here's some Vampire ashes&quot; <br /> &quot;....&quot; <br /> &quot;We're hunting this guy who's real bad. He sells children to politicians&quot; <br /> &quot;Ah, I was wondering where that guy was hiding. Right. Shut it down. The senator wants his kids.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the NSA. <br /> Really, the game is called the Masquerade, and elders have ever been paranoid about technology. It'd be surprising if not every prince didn't issue an edict about using electronics to mention critical information, or if neonates weren't worried their texts would be found and used as a pretext to execute them as masquerade breakers. Just because a book hasn't mentioned it, doesn't mean that all the elders are stupid, and just because players are frequently idiots with risky behaviour, doesn't mean that characters who've been living an unlife and who routinely steal blood from other people are equally stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T03:47:22-07:00","id":1457381,"title":"","content":"I'd expect a Camarilla-Anarch split to be born from technology, not hunters and a sudden need for an elite exclusionary club. The Ivory Tower declares that in the interests of preserving the Masquerade in an era of rapidly deplenishing privacy, all of your uage and data is to be monitored. Anybody who doesn't comply is considered in violation of the First Tradition. No this doesn't apply to your elders. This is for your own good, now hand over the smartphone neonate.<br /> <br /> And then the Anarchs, who have been pioneering all these little eperiments over the free web with technomancy tell them to get fucked and things go downhill from there.<br /> <br /> Or, more likely, the Camarilla never gives an edict and just starts quietly spying on everybody, the Anarchs go even harder for the cyber-rebellion hacking stuff, and the bickering and sect wars spread onto the net.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the NSA thinking vampires and wraiths are the same thing and tht thing is some kind of interdimensional alien is, for some reason, more interesting than them actually knowing anything about vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-22-2021, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T04:23:40-07:00","id":1457383,"title":"","content":"Not really. The Ivory tower is really a hands off form of goverment, with 90% of power in the hands of local municipalities. The Cam operates on the consent of it's princes and has limited ability to enforce it's wishes among the thousands of princedoms, and essentially can't be too domineering lest princes succeed. Another issue is, obviously collecting your data so that they can watch for things that will alert mortal authorities who are also collecting data is... extremely counterproductive, and absolutely nobody would agree to it. What you're describing is farcical and any prince that tries such a thing would go down, and while you might like that tone with your game, because moustache twirling evil-stupid villains are fun, it doesn't sit well with verisimilitude. <br /> <br /> The thing is, the Camarilla is, in fact, a sect that was created as a necessity for Modernity. It's not a coincidence that the Camarilla, Sabbat and Giovanni were all created at the start of modernity, and that there aren't medieval or classical sects (cults excluded). The founders of the Cam were in a time of relatively rapid technological change: Crossbows were out, Guns were in, cities were urbanizing rapidly, merchants became powerful and the world became more connected, fuedal systems declined, globe-spanning empires became a thing, and a whole load of other massive changes. The Anarchs popped up because they adapted first and grew from these new changes, and the Camarilla was created to steer things in a favourable direction for vampires during these times. While the Cam gets strained in the much-more rapidly changing 20th/21st century, it shouldn't just fucking break, because it was literally designed for modernity and honestly, computers aren't that hard to wrap your head around, especially if you're immortal and loaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T04:42:55-07:00","id":1457385,"title":"","content":"The tone I like in my games is totally ignoring everything V5 did to the Camarilla. Especially the stuff about tech. But if V5 splits the Camarilla and wants to start drawing modern parallels to big corporations and governments and elite vs anarchists and activists (or whatever they're trying to do), I would expect them to be depicted as data monitoring their people right next to the human organisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-22-2021, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T05:01:32-07:00","id":1457387,"title":"","content":"One can imagine Kindred from each sect deriving a lot of information security just from its own respective subcultural jargon, with different generations within each using even further differentiated vocabularies. The sample lexicons given in a lot of the old faction supplements would be just a starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T16:24:26-07:00","id":1457433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457385#post1457385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone I like in my games is totally ignoring everything V5 did to the Camarilla. Especially the stuff about tech. But if V5 splits the Camarilla and wants to start drawing modern parallels to big corporations and governments and elite vs anarchists and activists (or whatever they're trying to do), I would expect them to be depicted as data monitoring their people right next to the human organisations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing 1st generation Vampire: The Masquerade. That IS the game. Where did you get the idea it wasn't about rich assholes vs. poor assholes? I mean, it's Gothic PUNK. It's in the name.<br /> <br /> I feel like I sometimes live in a very different world than other players and Storytellers because for me the central conflict of Vampire: The Masquerade has always been the corrupt, greedy, evil Elders who want to fuck up your life and the poor disadvantaged Neonates who are caught up in their games. The Camarilla has never NOT been a bunch of insular assholes who call Blood Hunts for the slightest provocation because they don't like sharing with a bunch of good for nothing 13th generation who decide biting Rhianna would be a great idea even though Rhianna is YOUR vessel.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat? The Sabbat are an ANNOYANCE who get in the way of this central conflict.<br /> <br /> The only difference between the Sabbat and the Camarilla being that instead of calling Blood Hunts, the Sabbat just send its unwanted Neonates on Crusades. If they die? Good. If they don't die, they conquer territory and that benefits you as well.<br /> <br /> Praise Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T16:34:51-07:00","id":1457434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457433#post1457433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're describing 1st generation Vampire: The Masquerade. That IS the game. Where did you get the idea it wasn't about rich assholes vs. poor assholes? I mean, it's Gothic PUNK. It's in the name.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I know what the theme of the game is </i>. The bit I was poking at was the shift in this edition with the Camarilla now totally isolating and the Anarchs not within it. What is it now? Before it was the government. What is it now, a country club?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat? The Sabbat are an ANNOYANCE who get in the way of this central conflict. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat can convey the same themes of old vs young with a different tone if you want a change of pace, which makes them worthwhile additions. They are an addition, not an annoyance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-22-2021, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T16:35:24-07:00","id":1457435,"title":"","content":"Re: Vampire: The Masquerade and Hunters<br /> <br /> Hunters have been a major part of Vampire: The Masquerade but were weirdly the one thing excluded from <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> and that was really strange. I also felt The Hunter's Hunted II downgraded their dangerousness when Project: Twilight was upgrading it. Hunters are one of the very basic things about vampire mythology and we have them in Carmilla and Dracula as a major part of the storyline. Polidori's The Vampyre has a complete moron who utterly fails at hunting but that's also technically part of the story.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the Second Inquisition is there not to utterly upend the series but just to make the Masquerade seem more important as a concept. Some players acted like the worst stereotypes of Sabbat because they didn't think Hunters or the Prince were a proper threat. Giving the government flame-throwers, thermal vision, and M4A1s to unload into vampire hunters makes them less of a joke.<br /> <br /> Project: Twilight had a pretty good write-up of the government becoming more aware and more dangerous to vampirekind that could easily have led to the Second Inquisition. The Masquerade being broken was something very possible. V20, in one of the few critcisms I have of it, really didn't like this. It's why we had ANARCHS UNBOUND have the idea that suddenly Blood Magic was powerful enough and widespread enough that the internet couldn't be used to track down vampires.<br /> <br /> I know when vampires are exposed, there's no game. It's Game OverTM but I felt that was a silly solution. Indeed, the handling of humans is about my ONLY complaint about V20 that was otherwise an immensely solid game, Anarchs Unbound was a great book and helped reform the Anarchs from the idiotic way they treatyed by Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T16:37:19-07:00","id":1457436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457434#post1457434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>I know what the theme of the game is </i>. The bit I was poking at was the shift in this edition with the Camarilla now isolating and the Anarchs not within it. What is it now? Before it was the government. What is it now, a country club?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. I suppose it's more, &quot;We're trying to get rid of the rabble completely now&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat can convey the same themes of old vs young with a different tone if you want a change of pace, which makes them worthwhile additions. They are an addition, not an annoyance. </div> </div> </div>True-true. They are my second favorite sect after all. The Camarilla comes in third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T16:45:11-07:00","id":1457527,"title":"","content":"Some of my design notes for V5 games and the inquisition, mostly a list of hard idea's I applied and gave to players to show I plan to run them. Apologies if they're a little fragmented. I've edited out some stuff for my specific players but I hope they provide some useful suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1)The second inquisition not a unified front but a series of differant govermental organization engaging in low key co-operation and is often obstructed by realpolitik. For example Firstlight has deliberatly kept information on compromised russian politicians from the 8th directorate due to mutual distrust. The society of leopold and other theocratic sects are the only ones which operate pan nationaly and they have to tread lightly.<br /> <br /> 2) The level of effectiveness of 2nd inquisition organizations success rate varies greatly nation to nation, The United kingdom and Austria being most succesful with Russia and India lagging far behind. Several misguided or corrupt goverments are currently directly engaged in covert negotiations with the Carmarilla and Ashirra sects to see if some sort of backdoor agreement can be made. some countries have no formal goverment vampire hunt on.<br /> <br /> 3) Goverment approaches to the Vampiric menace are not limited to engage and destroy missions and economic pressure is being applied where possible. EG aggresive crack downs on sex industry in area's were is has been infiltrated or the dissolution of certain corporations.<br /> <br /> 4) Most vampire hunters institutions are so black op that they often cannot rely on local authorities co-operation and fear of infiltration means it's likely to stay that way.<br /> <br /> 5) while various institutions are making progress on the knowledgue of the vampiric world, their's still a dangerous lack of understanding or multiple levels. For example Necromancy is still a total unknown Leading to heavy losses when engaging Heceta vampires due to ignorance of wraiths and the underworld.<br /> <br /> 6) The second inquisition has made some feelers into attacking other supernatural groups and outreach to others at the same time a number of factions are aware of the decline in vampire power and are moving in for the kill. For example the British Verbenna/order of hermes are directly backing SO13 resulting in heavy casualties in clan Tremere and the total anihilation of all british house Carna. By contrast House red crest has had several of their kinfolk disapear into 8th directorate cells and one high profile termination of a sept elder. Israels unit 8211 prioritzies Fallen over kindred. The outusider only group institutionally involved<br /> <br /> 7) Sect responses have been from passive masquarade re-enforcement. Sabbat and Anarchs have formed ad hoc kill teams to engage and destroy hunters, when possible Sabbat have gone so far to create Templar units with this in mind. The Carmarilla has been engaging in institutional subversion and back door deals where possible. The Sabbat has also began taking the masquarade a lot more seriously.<br /> <br /> 8)Anarchs are the most vulnrable sect with their lack of institutional influence, bad organization and their overt affiliation with radical political groups. The Sabbats casualty rate is probably highest overall in the initial period but now the sect is reacting numbers are flattening.<br /> <br /> 9)Clan casualties vary greatly, the most heavy hit are Caitiff since their lack of suport and inexperiance, this will be something of a break in V5 meta but the Caitiff have been largely exterminated as easy targets. Least hard hit clan is clan Ravnos as their nomadic nature, low numbers and survivalist mentality has meant they've largely slipt under the radar.<br /> <br /> 10)Some forms of influence and infiltration of human power structures is more likely to draw inquisition attention than others.Typically localized corporations and ironically crime syndicates are far safer than civic services or goverment for example. National Military is probably the most likely to generate attention.<br /> <br /> 11)Some goverments have been making moves to weaponize vampires, while they've had no real successes with pure blooded Vampires. Thin bloods have proven to have real potential....<br /> <br /> hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T17:37:01-07:00","id":1457529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457527#post1457527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Israels unit 8211 prioritzies Fallen over kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally it seems sound, but this piece here irked me more than anything. The Jews in the forum may have a different and more appropriate opinion, but as far as I know this makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> On a religious/philosophical sense, demons aren't a thing in Judaism. Like, they're simply not there. The nearest thing a jew could fear would be a Wraith, since the dead sometimes doing stuff from Sheol, AFAIK, is at least part of jew folklore if not theology.<br /> <br /> Then, well, that seems to be a vampiric war raging in their neighborhood? Even if the elders aren't gathering at the Fertile Crescent <i>per se</i>, it is far more pressing to them from a strategic and geopolitical perspective. And there could be Ashirra backing up the Palestinians. Also, demons aren't a thing, but Caine and the Deluge are.<br /> <br /> Demons are pretty much a Christian concept. Even Shaitan/Iblis in Islam isn't nearly as prominent as demons are for Christians. The countries where it would make more sense for the hunters to focus on the Fallen above vampires would be the strongly Christian ones, like Italy, Brazil and US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T16:07:08-07:00","id":1457610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457529#post1457529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally it seems sound, but this piece here irked me more than anything. The Jews in the forum may have a different and more appropriate opinion, but as far as I know this makes absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> On a religious/philosophical sense, demons aren't a thing in Judaism. Like, they're simply not there. The nearest thing a jew could fear would be a Wraith, since the dead sometimes doing stuff from Sheol, AFAIK, is at least part of jew folklore if not theology.<br /> <br /> Then, well, that seems to be a vampiric war raging in their neighborhood? Even if the elders aren't gathering at the Fertile Crescent <i>per se</i>, it is far more pressing to them from a strategic and geopolitical perspective. And there could be Ashirra backing up the Palestinians. Also, demons aren't a thing, but Caine and the Deluge are.<br /> <br /> Demons are pretty much a Christian concept. Even Shaitan/Iblis in Islam isn't nearly as prominent as demons are for Christians. The countries where it would make more sense for the hunters to focus on the Fallen above vampires would be the strongly Christian ones, like Italy, Brazil and US.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah that part should have been edited out as it refers to our local cinematic WoD universe. Gehenna was cancelled by the 2nd inquisition and the return of Ynoch following the events the enosch Sarcophagus resulting in the deaths or incapacitation of several ancients including the Eldest in new york. Jerusalem is something of a hotzone area of Lucifarian/Reconciler conflicts following a chronicle back in 2011 and at the same time Israel occult/hunter circles are predictably wary of a group with strong links to the historical inquisition. The israeli's thoughts on the fallen are to presume them to be some sort of weird monster which lies a lot and could be mistaken for angels but isnt one.<br /> <br /> But it's only a rough waypoint so feel free to tinker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-24-2021, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T23:03:59-07:00","id":1457690,"title":"","content":"I always went with the idea that 'Gehenna' was really cyclical and perhaps only the higher generations saw it as final (a misunderstanding or a deception) and whatever was 'different' or problematic about this cycle ultimately resolved itself (for me it was a larger 'decline of magic' that finally saw even Vampires running out of magic to live on, hence they're decline in the original conception) But the cycle more or less passed like it always did (even if the damage from that cycle hasn't) and the second inquisition was part of the fallout from the latest cycle - which meant an elevated awareness about vampires from humanity in general (which plays into the Second Inquisition.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T23:08:28-07:00","id":1457691,"title":"","content":"People have always been predicting the end of the world. When the due date comes and nothing happens, they just push the date forward. It controls people. I'm actually a little dissapointed there are Gehenna scenarios and it wasn't all just a fun jab at certain religious groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T22:34:50-07:00","id":1457757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457529#post1457529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a religious/philosophical sense, demons aren't a thing in Judaism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am coming in WAY late and what I'm about to say might be either irrelevant or already addressed, but that hasn't stopped me yet! Also keep in mind Demon is the game I'm least familiar with and my knowledge is shaky at best. That said, here goes.<br /> <br /> I could easily see a situation where Isreali hunters focusing more on demons than vampires, not because of religious preconseptions and beliefs, but because of experience. Because Isreal isn't just important to the Judeo in Judeo-Christian religions, but also the Christian aspect. Jeruselam particularly as the site of Jesus's ministry and close to his eventual death-resurrection would make it a very key place for demons to go after for any number of reasons (in my head, I'm picturing Fallen going relic hunting around there) due to its historic importance. Meanwhile Kindred would have equally as many reasons to avoid the area (True Faith would presumably be much more common around there).<br /> <br /> It's just off the top of my head stuff, but I don't see a real problem with it just because Judaism doesn't have demons. No religion has a belief system involving vampires either, but hunters focus on them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T23:43:06-07:00","id":1457759,"title":"","content":"You have very fair points, and the question is addressed already by Ragged Robin next post, but let me elaborate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457757#post1457757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily see a situation where Isreali hunters focusing more on demons than vampires, not because of religious preconseptions and beliefs</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to take this out of the way in case someone mistake what I'm saying, but that goes without saying. I'll focus on the question if this is a good option in general, not if it can be done. It can, totally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457757#post1457757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as the site of Jesus's ministry and close to his eventual death-resurrection would make it a very key place for demons to go after for any number of reasons (in my head, I'm picturing Fallen going relic hunting around there) due to its historic importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how Demon works. Since you said you're not that familiar, let me summarize.<br /> <br /> D:tF focus on two main moments, before the Imprisonment and after Escaping. The first occurs in a Time Before Time fashion, so it links to no particular place and as their war was worldwide, things from that time can be found all around the world. A relic from the War is as likely to be in the Levant as in the Moon. The second was 22 years ago, so figures.<br /> <br /> In the mean time Lucifer and the Earthbound were wandering the Earth in one fashion or another, and D:tF does say that their hands are likely to be at any and all religious movement, since their main resource is Faith, but that ultimately also means that even the Abrahamic religions didn't got such a special attention. Demons do recognize that they have a stronger &quot;memory&quot; of past events, but in general their history among religions don't place them as more likely to be linked to relics or something.<br /> <br /> So Israel have no particular significance to D:tF as a whole. It is certain that some Demons may search for answers there, but not a lot more than anywhere else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457757#post1457757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile Kindred would have equally as many reasons to avoid the area (True Faith would presumably be much more common around there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire deal far more with the area since the beginning of the game. Almost every clan traces its origin to the region or its neighborhood, it was the main hub of Cainite activity in the ancient world, and it still have a strong presence of vampires.<br /> <br /> Most glaring, in V5 there was a frigging vampire war in the area, with elders from far and wild feeling a pull to the region, the Sabbat going to war there <i>en masse</i>, Antedilluvians and stuff all over the place. So it was <u><b>officially</b></u> teeming with vampires regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457757#post1457757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isreal isn't just important to the Judeo in Judeo-Christian religions</div> </div> </div> </div>Jerusalem is important to three big religious branches, not two. But the two that live there in big numbers aren't Christians. This isn't just something in the setting, this is something in the real world, where real people live and consume these games. In an in-game perspective, the Israeli military focusing on Demons seems contrived if there is no explicit event leading to it. In an out-of-game perspective this would left a bad taste in the mouths of two huge ethnic groups that historically don't have a lot of reasons to feel nice and cuddly with Christians hijacking their stories AGAIN.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the post I was answering to was about design notes for the game, not a personal chronicle. Ragged Robin explained that this piece was left there by accident precisely because it was actually about local gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T02:03:54-07:00","id":1457766,"title":"","content":"Demons aren't a thing in Judaism?<br /> <br /> Yes and no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shedim\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Compendium_rarissimum_totius_Artis_Magicae._Wellcome_L0027769.jpg/960px-Compendium_rarissimum_totius_Artis_Magicae._Wellcome_L0027769.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shedim\" target=\"_blank\"> Shedim - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shedim\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shedim </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T02:50:07-07:00","id":1457770,"title":"","content":"To be much more clear on that:<br /> <br /> Demons as fallen angels that serve the devil against the heavenly host aren't a thing in Judaism.<br /> <br /> Demons as a broad term for malevolent spiritual entities could be applied in translation to some being in Jewish culture.<br /> <br /> Since the topic is around Demon: the Fallen, the &quot;no&quot; is a lot more relevant than the &quot;yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course the topic was also sparked by talk of an Israeli military unit, not some Jewish equivalent to the Society of Leopold. This means it really isn't going to preoccupy itself with Rabbinic thought n how to classify monsters; it would be focused on adapting to fighting the creatures they're ware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T05:28:28-07:00","id":1457779,"title":"","content":"There really aren't that many Jews in the world, so a &quot;Jewish&quot; themed hunter team would feel to some small degree like Tokenism for me. An Isreali unit would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T10:56:07-07:00","id":1457802,"title":"","content":"As well, there's already the Lions of Zion in the books. While a mage organization, it's a purely Jewish faith based one centered primarily around keeping (Orthodox) Jewish communities safe from (other) supernatural influences. They're already what a Jewish version of the SoL would look like (even if like the SoL have some fundamental writing issues that can make them more farcical than satirical). Being part of Mage helps avoid the tokenism (or worse, because there's a minefield of anti-Semitic dog-whistles when it comes to secret Jewish organizations operating above the law) because Mage is full of small Crafts that focus on the communities built around their faiths and traditions rather than wanting to be part of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Though, that said, it is kind of weird to assert that a Jewish organization is tokenism when an Israeli organization isn't... when there's a lot more Jews in the world than Israelis. It's also very hard to imagine an Israeli governmental &quot;hunter&quot; organization that isn't just a Technocracy run thing But that's partially because people tend to equate Israel with Jerusalem and thus religion and faith, but don't really appreciate how much (a) modern Jerusalem outside the walls of the Old City is a bustling political city with all the secular concerns of life still very much part of the character of the city and (b) that the rest of the country's major population centers are much more secular and modern in character.<br /> <br /> The State of Israel is probably one of the most Technocracy friendly governments in the world. Before the modern State of Israel was even founded, Jerusalem Syndrome had already entered into the local social narratives as a way to dismiss all of the highly religious people drawn to the area because of the importance of Jerusalem to so many religious people globally. Getting labelled as suffering Jerusalem Syndrome means you'll be treated as seriously regarding faith as a Time Square Elmo will be regarding childhood education.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T12:08:19-07:00","id":1457809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457779#post1457779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really aren't that many Jews in the world, so a &quot;Jewish&quot; themed hunter team would feel to some small degree like Tokenism for me. An Isreali unit would be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it depends on how large the group is. There's only a 100,000 or so vampires in the world (unless you believe in dramatic overcrowding). The SAD was composed of like 30 guys.<br /> <br /> I can get 30 Jewish guys together in my town that is the ass end of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T15:34:16-07:00","id":1457835,"title":"","content":"In our games the previously mentioned Lions of Zion are the default anti-monster faction for Jewish communities, which is mega bad news since they're awakened mages. Their response in game hasnt really been fleshed out but I imagine they might just presume they're lying considering the fragmented nature of Fallen recollections<br /> <br /> <br /> On a local level the other default is the Vigil style Cells which I tend to generate if any community is too pressured/infiltrated by supernatural groups. I'm giving serious thought to an intersectionalist disenfranchised centered hunter cell from recent writtings implying Anarchs are getting way to open in their associations with those groups.<br /> <br /> As a side for anyone interested in suggestions on Goverment anti-monster conspiracies I'd recommend the laundrette. Since it has a lot of good suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T20:03:08-07:00","id":1457853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457802#post1457802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also very hard to imagine an Israeli governmental &quot;hunter&quot; organization that isn't just a Technocracy run thing</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, and that is why I said it is totally doable. A high Demonic presence would be contrived without good reasoning, but the best reasoning would still be a completely secular one. The main problem here is that without further explanation the religious aspect comes to mind too easily, especially since we're talking D:tF.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I think that the main difficulty with treating Israel in dept, especially through a military unit, is precisely that it would call for treading Israeli politics, and that is a complicated matter. Not only that, but to talk properly about monster hunting in the region you must talk about the Palestinian conflict, at the very least because the monsters can (a) relate somehow to the conflict and (b) use it for their own ends.<br /> <br /> It isn't something I think we have to avoid, but as an ongoing ethnic and political conflict with a lot of complex nuances that few people are even aware of, it's a very delicate matter. In this, Demon seems like a risky splat to use for the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T23:15:31-07:00","id":1457868,"title":"","content":"I mean, the Technocracy doesn't &quot;run&quot; stuff much.<br /> <br /> I've always felt they are much more likely to arm a Hunter organization and cover up for it than do it themselves.<br /> <br /> Wheels within wheels, Boxes within Boxes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3cur1uMGrxs\" data-code=\"3cur1uMGrxs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3cur1uMGrxs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T02:43:13-07:00","id":1457880,"title":"","content":"The problem with the whole &quot;boxes within boxes&quot; thing is that it sounds great for a spooky conspiracy the audience will never have to be sold on as a functional organization once you peek under the flaps. It neglects that for exerting any serious amount of control like this there's a level of infrastructure and numbers that you can't effectively scale below. Israel is certainly an outlier because it punches way above its weight-class in terms of population to geopolitical importance. A small enough group of Technocrats to hide with all those layers of conspiracy in a country as small as Israel is also too few agents to actually handle all the major things that need dealt with (even more so with the canon status of the Middle East in the WoD). One of the reasons to commit to a larger presence that's too big to rely on the &quot;we just nudge from the shadows&quot; idea, is also that Israel is a great staging group for agents that primarily work in neighboring countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T03:05:52-07:00","id":1457883,"title":"","content":"I mean it's probably worth noting the Union explicitly protects the masquarade so they might even hamstring modern hunters attempts to find vampires by covering vampiric activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T13:36:48-07:00","id":1457921,"title":"","content":"The books generally present the situation as being very dependent on how the Technocrats view a given hunter group's methods. A group that keeps to the shadows and kills RDs while maintaining the secret of the supernatural of normal humans is likely to see non-interference or even help from the Union. A group that's trying to expose the supernatural to the world in the hopes of humans rising up against them are likely to be shocked at how easily they're discredited and ignored without ever noticing the NWO's operation to shut them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T14:28:33-07:00","id":1457922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457880#post1457880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the whole &quot;boxes within boxes&quot; thing is that it sounds great for a spooky conspiracy the audience will never have to be sold on as a functional organization once you peek under the flaps. It neglects that for exerting any serious amount of control like this there's a level of infrastructure and numbers that you can't effectively scale below. Israel is certainly an outlier because it punches way above its weight-class in terms of population to geopolitical importance. A small enough group of Technocrats to hide with all those layers of conspiracy in a country as small as Israel is also too few agents to actually handle all the major things that need dealt with (even more so with the canon status of the Middle East in the WoD). One of the reasons to commit to a larger presence that's too big to rely on the &quot;we just nudge from the shadows&quot; idea, is also that Israel is a great staging group for agents that primarily work in neighboring countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some suspension of disbelief is necessary for the idea that our world is secretly ruled by science wizards and vampires both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T14:43:21-07:00","id":1457923,"title":"","content":"Which is why I pointed out the difference between a vague shadowy group the players will never interact with beyond some puppet representative, and a group like the Camarilla or Technocracy where you're actually expected to be able to play members of the conspiracy and the ST is expect to actually make the leadership believable.<br /> <br /> Suspension of disbelief isn't a panacea for fiction writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T15:54:42-07:00","id":1457926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457923#post1457923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I pointed out the difference between a vague shadowy group the players will never interact with beyond some puppet representative, and a group like the Camarilla or Technocracy where you're actually expected to be able to play members of the conspiracy and the ST is expect to actually make the leadership believable.<br /> <br /> Suspension of disbelief isn't a panacea for fiction writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is, frankly, why I run my Vampire and Mage games in separate universes.<br /> <br /> In my vampire game there are no \u201cMages\u201d (in the MtA sense; linear sorcerers, true faith, demon worship and agencies using experimental tech exist, but there\u2019s no war for reality in my Vampire campaign) or \u201cWerewolves\u201d (there are Lupines, savage flesh-eating monsters cursed by the bite of another Lupine who claim Lycaon as their founder in the same way Vampires claim Caine)<br /> <br /> The \u201cTechnocracy\u201d that destroyed the Ravnos Antediluvian in my Vampire game was basically the \u201cFive Eyes\u201d Intel community, the nukes were conventional and when that failed someone was actually willing to listen to the Project Twilight crew and try using a hastily repurposed solar mirror from an off the books Znamya-like solar power project.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been two decades and the Intel community has basically forgotten it even happened... a lot of Cam elders burned a lot of capital making sure the entire thing is buried under so much red tape in so many independent intelligence silos and classification layers followed by virtually everyone involved in the incident being \u201cpersuaded\u201d to take early retirements that only Project Twilight\u2019s heirs even know there WAS an incident beyond the official cover story.<br /> <br /> It makes my Vampire campaign run a LOT smoother when I don\u2019t have to worry about Mage and Garou shenanigans invading it.<br /> <br /> (Conversely, in my Mage campaign vampires are mostly solitary hunters and there are no sects or Antediluvians or similar elements that take the focus off the conflict between the Mage factions... the Etherites do however have a theory that parallel Earths where different supernatural paradigms dominate exist... which is how any crossover I might ever run would actually work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T17:06:13-07:00","id":1457928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457923#post1457923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I pointed out the difference between a vague shadowy group the players will never interact with beyond some puppet representative, and a group like the Camarilla or Technocracy where you're actually expected to be able to play members of the conspiracy and the ST is expect to actually make the leadership believable.<br /> <br /> Suspension of disbelief isn't a panacea for fiction writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that's part of the problem isn't it? Because the Technocracy SHOULD be shadowy and the upper levels of the Camarilla SHOULD be secretive.<br /> <br /> You should know your Prince and Comptroller.<br /> <br /> Never know the Inner Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T20:00:44-07:00","id":1457947,"title":"","content":"Never meeting, or even knowing the names, of the Inner Council doesn't matter. The Inner Council doesn't have the control it does because they're a secret group of Elders, but because they have all of the combined resources of the Camarilla membership to put to use. Same with the Union. The Inner Council needs Princes to keep control over city governments if they want to enact larger plans. They &quot;nudge&quot; the stock market by using favor trading to get a Prince to use their power to direction cause an &quot;unexpected&quot; event to the Inner Council's benefit.<br /> <br /> PC Cam members are just inside the circle of knowledge that sees this as just doing business rather than some mysterious thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T22:01:21-07:00","id":1457955,"title":"","content":"I don't know that the upper echelons of the Camarilla should be secretive or unknown. I imagine most people know the names of most of the Justicars and likely at least some of the members of the Inner Council. I don't really view that as a problem since in most VtM games players will never be interacting with the leadership of the Camarilla anyway (most likely the local Prince and maybe an Archon are the highest ranked Camarilla members most PCs will ever meet). And if a Storyteller feels the need to introduce some shadowy level of rulership it's easy enough to spin some new conspiracy that is pulling the strings of the Camarilla or the Inner Council or whatever (indeed that was basically the point of the True Black Hand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-29-2021, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T14:11:02-07:00","id":1457993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457955#post1457955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that the upper echelons of the Camarilla should be secretive or unknown. I imagine most people know the names of most of the Justicars and likely at least some of the members of the Inner Council. I don't really view that as a problem since in most VtM games players will never be interacting with the leadership of the Camarilla anyway (most likely the local Prince and maybe an Archon are the highest ranked Camarilla members most PCs will ever meet). And if a Storyteller feels the need to introduce some shadowy level of rulership it's easy enough to spin some new conspiracy that is pulling the strings of the Camarilla or the Inner Council or whatever (indeed that was basically the point of the True Black Hand).</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it's an organization that knows that once you have your name out there that you will become a target. The Camarilla exists based on preserving secrecy and you don't want a Neonate telling a Hunter who tells the Inquisition what the name of the Ventrue Inner Councilman is.<br /> <br /> In my games, no one outside of an Elder even knows what a Justicar is in most cases let alone who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T20:08:28-07:00","id":1458012,"title":"","content":"But here's the problem:<br /> <br /> An Archon comes to town to deal with an issue. How does anyone know that the Archon is who they say they are, if nobody knows who the Justicars that empower the Archons are?<br /> <br /> The Inner Council's direct operatives all exert a huge amount of power on reputation alone. Most of them were famous among vampires before getting to those positions: like Theo Bell (even with V5's metaplot, Theo Bell is not a shadowy figure nobody knows about). What replaces that if you make them more anonymous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T21:22:16-07:00","id":1458015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457993#post1457993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because it's an organization that knows that once you have your name out there that you will become a target. The Camarilla exists based on preserving secrecy and you don't want a Neonate telling a Hunter who tells the Inquisition what the name of the Ventrue Inner Councilman is.<br /> <br /> In my games, no one outside of an Elder even knows what a Justicar is in most cases let alone who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;So, I heard you Brujah are leaving the Camarilla. How's that going to work out for you?&quot;<br /> &quot;We're leaving the Camarilla? Says who?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, the Brujah guy who was on the Inner Council.&quot;<br /> &quot;There was a Brujah guy on the Inner Council? What the fuck is an inner council? And why does it matter what he says anyway?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well it means you guys won't have a Justicar anymore.&quot;<br /> &quot;... the fuck is a Justicar? Seriously, is this some kind of joke?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-30-2021, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T22:24:57-07:00","id":1458019,"title":"","content":"The big problem with the Camarilla is that their entire concept went through several changes throughout the years, and the games pretend it wasn't the case. In the beginning it was a conspiracy theory about someone pulling the strings of Princes and Primogen all over the world, but no organization truly extended from one city to the next in any formal fashion. Then it became an open ideology, still with any formal structure being just a conspiracy theory. Then an association. Then Vampire UN, and only after a time as UN they became a formal government with a structured administrative body.<br /> <br /> So the Camarilla was all this at some time and, weirdly, all of them are somehow canon simultaneously, because the books never admitted a retcon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T23:17:44-07:00","id":1458023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458015#post1458015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;So, I heard you Brujah are leaving the Camarilla. How's that going to work out for you?&quot;<br /> &quot;We're leaving the Camarilla? Says who?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, the Brujah guy who was on the Inner Council.&quot;<br /> &quot;There was a Brujah guy on the Inner Council? What the fuck is an inner council? And why does it matter what he says anyway?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well it means you guys won't have a Justicar anymore.&quot;<br /> &quot;... the fuck is a Justicar? Seriously, is this some kind of joke?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Humorously, yeah, pretty much.<br /> <br /> I would also add:<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, the Brujah are part of the Camarilla. I thought we were the Anarchs.&quot;<br /> &quot;The Gangrel left the Camarilla too.&quot;<br /> &quot;When were the Gangrel part of the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> &quot;The Nineties?&quot;<br /> &quot;Fuck man, that was like thirty years ago!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T23:44:45-07:00","id":1458024,"title":"","content":"I think the books, authors, and most fans ignore that retconning because 99% of it happened between 1e and early 2e. Even then, it less of a straight progression through those modes, and a messy jumble of ideas that got sorted out. Children of the Inquisition from 1992 already established Karsh and two members of the Camarilla Inner Circle detailed in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T00:54:05-07:00","id":1458029,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the ideas are still mixed there. Yes, most of it happened early in the game. I wouldn't say 99% because the last stage did took some time to be fleshed out, but that's just a detail. The problem is the last bit, it is still all that at once simultaneously. The ideas and themes were never weeded out even when they started to contradict themselves, so Camarilla elders are simultaneously hyper secretive and famous politicians, for example.<br /> <br /> I'd say that partly the problem is precisely that it happened so early in the game that most people just got used to how the setting is, contradictions and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T01:01:19-07:00","id":1458032,"title":"","content":"I feel like this discussion should really be in a different thread, but to me, the best thing we could do is change the response to Xaviers's King Curtis style &quot;WE R leAving&quot; from &quot;oh we've left the Cam?&quot; to &quot;Oh, we need a new Justicar and someone on the inner circle, but I don't know if we've got anyone who's easy to convince to join the latter, this may take a while.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Brujah on the otherhand have the issue of too many vampires wanting the position. Being a violent clan, A bloodbath ensues. <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel the schismatics really need an uphill fight to to get into the Cam's upper strata. They fit in V5 because half of them are strongly religious and the Cam are Republicans, but in the grand scheme of things, they don't. They're religiously divided, there's great historical enmity, there's the issue of the clan feeling that it has a right to be Judge, Jury and executioner, there's a great many diablerists and those who aren't on the path of humanity, and there's also their small presence/the fact that they are absent from most Cam cities. The Bribes and Benefits they offer likely aren't that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T16:30:57-07:00","id":1458268,"title":"","content":"i tended to work on the assumption the inner circle was secret but the overall structure of the Carmarilla wasnt. On reflection it's ultimatly a fuedal system in terms of structure except with the Inner council as a monarch. Conversly the Anarch's are bassically fragemented tribes if I'm feeling generous which is why they're probably doomed at the hands of their three main enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T17:22:50-07:00","id":1458276,"title":"","content":"In simple terms, the Gangrel leaving makes sense because very few Gangrel Elders got anything out of the Camarilla to begin with.<br /> <br /> 800 year old guy in the woods doesn't visit Elysium very often.<br /> <br /> And the Neonates didn't get anything either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T18:49:46-07:00","id":1458288,"title":"","content":"Of course:<br /> <br /> 1) Lots of Gangrel aren't hermits, because they need to feed on humans.<br /> <br /> 2) Any Gangrel that value having a chunk of wilderness as their Domain better support the Cam to make use of the powerful network of money and influence to keep those bits of wilderness from getting sold to developers, miners, or whatever.<br /> <br /> 3) Any Gangrel that wants to be free to do their thing off in the woods benefits directly from the Cam's hardest stance on keeping vampire populations small, and defending territories from Sabbat attacks so lone Gangrel don't get stomped (or eaten) by a few nomadic packs. Or from Tremere looking for new test subjects for a new form of Gargoyles that are easier to hide from modern tech.<br /> <br /> But sure, that's &quot;nothing&quot; for the Gangrel to see as upsides to being in the Cam even if they're not interested in trying to fight the Ventrue and Toreador over petty politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T19:18:31-07:00","id":1458290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458288#post1458288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course:<br /> <br /> 1) Lots of Gangrel aren't hermits, because they need to feed on humans.<br /> <br /> 2) Any Gangrel that value having a chunk of wilderness as their Domain better support the Cam to make use of the powerful network of money and influence to keep those bits of wilderness from getting sold to developers, miners, or whatever.<br /> <br /> 3) Any Gangrel that wants to be free to do their thing off in the woods benefits directly from the Cam's hardest stance on keeping vampire populations small, and defending territories from Sabbat attacks so lone Gangrel don't get stomped (or eaten) by a few nomadic packs. Or from Tremere looking for new test subjects for a new form of Gargoyles that are easier to hide from modern tech.<br /> <br /> But sure, that's &quot;nothing&quot; for the Gangrel to see as upsides to being in the Cam even if they're not interested in trying to fight the Ventrue and Toreador over petty politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think your argument is working but it actually underscores a huge chunk of why the Camarilla is worthless to them.<br /> <br /> 1] Yes and there's plenty of these in the Wilderness and surrounding edge of domains.<br /> <br /> 2] If you think the Gangrel rely on the CAMARILLA to adjudicate their domains versus themselves, you have utterly misrepresented their culture.<br /> <br /> 3] Except the Camarilla relies on the GANGREL to enforce their protection from the Sabbat not the other way around. Which is a major reason why the Gangrel left according to Lore of the Clans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T19:42:56-07:00","id":1458292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458290#post1458290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think your argument is working but it actually underscores a huge chunk of why the Camarilla is worthless to them.<br /> <br /> 1] Yes and there's plenty of these in the Wilderness and surrounding edge of domains.<br /> <br /> 2] If you think the Gangrel rely on the CAMARILLA to adjudicate their domains versus themselves, you have utterly misrepresented their culture.<br /> <br /> 3] Except the Camarilla relies on the GANGREL to enforce their protection from the Sabbat not the other way around. Which is a major reason why the Gangrel left according to Lore of the Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where in Lore of the Clans does it say the things you are saying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T21:03:30-07:00","id":1458297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458290#post1458290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think your argument is working but it actually underscores a huge chunk of why the Camarilla is worthless to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're responses need to be a lot more thorough to hold to this position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1] Yes and there's plenty of these in the Wilderness and surrounding edge of domains. </div> </div> </div>Less and less every year, and more and more spread out. Over 55% of global humans live in a city. That jumps up to 75% when you include suburbs and other smaller municipalities. That's expected to get even more crowded in the next twenty years (it's already much higher in highly developed countries).<br /> <br /> Then you have to account for the fact that wilderness also has Lupines in it, and Lore of the Clans is very adamant that that's a problem.<br /> <br /> Lore of the Clans also stresses that the Gangrel have adapted to the reality of needing to be urban predators. Just take a look at the sample concepts in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2] If you think the Gangrel rely on the CAMARILLA to adjudicate their domains versus themselves, you have utterly misrepresented their culture. </div> </div> </div>You're misunderstanding me. The Gangrel rely on their status as members of the Cam to keep the Cam from buying out the land they claim and selling it to humans to exploit for natural resources or to build housing on.<br /> <br /> Lore of the Clans repeatedly stresses that the Gangrel joined the Cam out of self-preservation; including from the Cam itself. Joining the Cam was in part to stop the Cam from wiping the Gangrel out using superior organization and numbers (and the Cam do have plenty of powerful individuals too).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3] Except the Camarilla relies on the GANGREL to enforce their protection from the Sabbat not the other way around. Which is a major reason why the Gangrel left according to Lore of the Clans. </div> </div> </div>I believe you're mistaking the content of the book. You seem to be referencing the reasons why the Gangrel ATs leave the Cam for the Sabbat, not what the Gangrel left the Cam to go Indie.<br /> <br /> And, again, LotC repeatedly points out how the Gangrel had to acknowledge that the Cam was a benefit to the Clan despite it rankling their culture and attitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T00:55:55-07:00","id":1458308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458292#post1458292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where in Lore of the Clans does it say the things you are saying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore of the Clans established that the Gangrel joined the Camarilla because the Gangrel felt they could use other clans as a defense against their enemies but gradually ended up being the front line instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T03:46:54-07:00","id":1458313,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;Gangrel live in the sticks and hate urban living&quot; thing is really a simplistic view on them. Yes, they can live away from civilization, the clan weakness indeed encourages <i>older </i>Gangrel to remain some distance away. Their natural disciplines don't have them thrive in the city as much as other clans do, which gives them a competitive disadvantage. <br /> <br /> First, the Gangrel aren't nature hippies, and only oppose urbanization when it's to the extent that other clans will have an advantage over them. People are the prefered source of food for any vampire, and so long as an area isn't stable and prosperous enough that the other clans have their attention drawn to it, the Gangrel will relish the development. A small city or large town where the Gangrel can easily squash any interloper without reprisal? Ideal. Most cities aren't big things with high vampire counts where vampires have to worry about politics. A Gangrel can excel in these small cities. <br /> <br /> Second, most young Gangrel aren't powerful enough to survive the wilds, but aren't yet inhuman enough to need to brave the wilds. As young vampires grossly outnumber older vampires, this is rather important. <br /> <br /> Third, and most importantly, in a city big enough for political organization, the Gangrel can easily leverage the skills they are good at to stake claim to a Domain that's legally protected. The reason why Gangrel so often live in the sticks is competition, but if the Government backs your claim, and you're not yet a chimera, why not take something nice in the inner city? The Camarilla is great for this because the Gangrel, in theory, have claims just as valid as any of the other 6 clans. <b>The Camarilla supports the Traditions, and the Traditions support the Gangrel more than they do many other clans</b>. <b>In an Anarch city, the Gangrel don't have laws to rely on, so their Territorial claims go out the window whenever a Brujah, Toreador or Ventrue wants the land: They simply can't compete with an equally aged member of those clans in the city</b>. (my God this realization makes me want to do a whole thread on why the gangrel leaving was dumb as fuck) <br /> <br /> <br /> There's one thing to note: <br /> Before the Camarilla, the Gangrel often railed against high clans and the establishment. They did the best in surviving the inquisition and the anarch revolt. Suspicious? Well, there's lots of rational reasons for it, but there's also plenty of excuses for the high clans were they to ever decide that one clan needed to be removed from existence. The Greatest threat to Gangrel was all the other clans banding against them in an age where cities were clearly the future. Joining the cam for their own protection was very much a necessity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T04:38:36-07:00","id":1458316,"title":"","content":"<b>The Second Inquisition and Modern Times</b><br /> <br /> Personally, I think the big reason for the existence of the Second Inquisition is due to the fact that so much of our relationship to conspiracy theories, government, surveillance, and so much else that was more &quot;believable&quot; in the Nineties has changed in the wake of the War on Terror. The dramatic increase in power of the state following 9/11 and during the War on Terror was only beginning when the Old World of Darkness was destroyed.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, it's hard to believe with cell phone tracking, social media, the NSA tapping all of our phones, and so on that it is hard for a secret organization of immortals like the Camarilla to exist without being detected by the government.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of ways you can deal with this kind of problem:<br /> <br /> 1:] <b>The Supernaturals Run Everything</b><br /> <br /> The Technocracy or Camarilla or both are completely in charge of global media with no real danger of the Masquerade ever being destroyed. I dislike this because it basically removes the central premise of the gameline.<br /> <br /> 2:] <b>Humanity is deeply stupid</b><br /> <br /> I mean, the way the Dresden Files does it.<br /> <br /> 3:] <b>Humanity is on it</b><br /> <br /> Which is kind of what the Second Inquisition is about. They may be hunting vampires but they're also keeping the existence of the undead secret while they're attempting to conduct their shadow war.<br /> <br /> I really liked the set up in PROJECT: TWILIGHT where the government was a mixture of incompetent and capable. The NSA was heavily compromised by the Tremere and Technocracy, the SAD was compromised by FOUR groups, and otehr secret societies but there were still dangerous agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T16:50:40-07:00","id":1458425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1457921#post1457921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books generally present the situation as being very dependent on how the Technocrats view a given hunter group's methods. A group that keeps to the shadows and kills RDs while maintaining the secret of the supernatural of normal humans is likely to see non-interference or even help from the Union. A group that's trying to expose the supernatural to the world in the hopes of humans rising up against them are likely to be shocked at how easily they're discredited and ignored without ever noticing the NWO's operation to shut them up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of Hunters, but on the inverse of the &quot;silent and keeping secret of the supernatural&quot; types, that reminds me: what ever happened to the Imbued?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:11:36-07:00","id":1458450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457097-are-there-traces-of-the-so-called-second-inquisition-in-v20?p=1458425#post1458425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Speaking of Hunters, but on the inverse of the &quot;silent and keeping secret of the supernatural&quot; types, that reminds me: what ever happened to the Imbued?</div> </div> </div> </div>They still exist; the Dhampir entry in BJD even mentions them as one of the few types of supernatural crossover they could actually become in addition to being a Dhampir... and since text is important, here's the quote;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Dhampir\u2019s vampiric heritage makes it impossible for her to become a changeling, demon, mage, mummy, werewolf, or their related kin. She can be blood bound to a vampire, though she does not become a ghoul. A Dhampir can become Imbued, but does not lose their Dhampir template.&quot;</i> -BJD, p. 144<br /> <br /> My general policy is that if something is stated to exist in V20, but there are no expressed mechanics for it in any of the X20 books, you can just use whatever the last extant version of it was... Hunter the Reckoning had only one edition so I'd just use that as is for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:35:25-07:00","id":1458452,"title":"","content":"That's strange on the part of BJD. The Messengers explicitly only imbued mundane humans with no pre-existing contact with the Supernatural at all. Though I guess its at least something on the Imbued, even though its a kinda iffy tidbit. Makes me rest ALL of the oWoD titles got a &quot;20th&quot; lift-up, but that'd never happen anyway..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:24:23-07:00","id":1458460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you wish to complain about a post then please report it. Mine as well as anyone's. But if you have a problem with a poster then you should not engage with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's the smartest hing i've seen you post. i'm gonna take that advise to heart","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:26:11-07:00","id":1458461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div 