\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T06:34:26-07:00","id":1458503,"title":"","content":"I'll put bluntly what my own take on the Second Inquisition is:<br /> <br /> They should had gone all-in. Masquerade was blown-up and that's it.<br /> <br /> Once the game proposes to move forward into Gehenna or post-Gehenna, then by all means it should have left the old themes behind and built new ones. It is a new game in a sense. The shit hit the fan and all that.<br /> <br /> And given the metaplot building of Revised, it was either that or ToJ was wrong, Gehenna isn't real and now lets tie up some things and go home. The themes change anyways, because the looming threat that was part of them is gone. No particularly big deal, but whatever, and the Masquerade stays as it was, since I do agree with Heavy Arms that it doesn't make a lot of sense under no PoV in the way it is now.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but this should be Go Big or Go Home. And it didn't either. They chose a metaplot that kinda got stuck in the middle, moving forward but not daring to cross lines. A lot of lines. That's cheap, and makes me feel like V5 can give me ideas, but in no way a proper setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","